# Firebase web config. NAMES ONLY — never commit the values.
#
# Where the values come from: Firebase console → Project settings → General → Your apps →
# SDK setup and configuration. Project is `notemaker-claude` (ticket 04).
#
# Locally: copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env*` is gitignored except this file.
# Deployed: set as Cloudflare Pages environment variables on BOTH Production and Preview
# (ticket 10), along with NODE_VERSION=20.
#
# These four ship inside the client bundle by necessity and cannot be hidden from a user of the
# app. That is NOT the same claim as "safe to commit" — this repo is public, and a value written
# here enters a permanently archived, continuously scanned index. Record the pointer, never the
# value. Enforcement lives in Firestore security rules, the Auth authorised-domain list, and the
# API key's HTTP-referrer restriction — never in secrecy of the key.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Running it locally
#
#   1. cp .env.example .env.local   (a .env.local may already exist holding
#      placeholder values — replace them; placeholders boot but cannot sign in)
#   2. npm install
#   3. npm run dev   ->   http://localhost:5173
#
# NEVER edit values into src/platform/firebase.ts. It reads only import.meta.env,
# so .env.local is the whole mechanism — nothing else needs touching, and a source
# file edited "just to test" is how a key reaches a commit. Vite reads .env.local
# at server start, so restart `npm run dev` after changing a value; HMR won't pick
# it up.
#
# The port is pinned (vite.config.ts, strictPort) because ticket 04's referrer
# restriction lists 5173 and 4173 explicitly and does not wildcard ports. If 5173
# is busy, Vite now REFUSES TO START rather than moving to 5174 — free the port,
# don't override it. Guarded by src/test/devServerPorts.test.ts.
#
# Rotating the API key (ticket 04): the new key goes in VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY
# here in .env.local, and in the Cloudflare Pages env vars. Nowhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
